@*
    Blazor's reconnect overlay, a <dialog> driven by Blazor's own state classes.

    Six states: first attempt, retrying with a countdown, failed (with a Retry button), paused by the server,
    resume failed (with a Resume button), and rejected (which reloads). Blazor drives all six
    by swapping a class on this element; the ids and class names below are the framework's and
    must not be renamed.

    The seventh line is this suite's addition rather than the framework's:
    session-guard.js adds .session-guard-reloading just before it reloads the page, which hides
    the "retry or reload yourself" copy and reveals "Restoring your session". The distinction
    matters to the reader — "failed, retry yourself" and "failed, recovering for you" call for
    different reactions, and the second is what actually happens after a redeploy.
*@
<script type="module" src="@Assets["Shared/ReconnectModal.razor.js"]"></script>

<dialog id="components-reconnect-modal" data-nosnippet>
    <div class="components-reconnect-container">
        <div class="components-rejoining-animation" aria-hidden="true">
            <div></div>
            <div></div>
        </div>
        <p class="components-reconnect-first-attempt-visible">
            Rejoining the server...
        </p>
        <p class="components-reconnect-repeated-attempt-visible">
            Rejoin failed... trying again in <span id="components-seconds-to-next-attempt"></span> seconds.
        </p>
        <p class="components-reconnect-failed-visible">
            Failed to rejoin.<br />Please retry or reload the page.
        </p>
        <p class="reconnect__reloading">
            Restoring your session&hellip;
        </p>
        <button id="components-reconnect-button" class="components-reconnect-failed-visible">
            Retry
        </button>
        <p class="components-pause-visible">
            The session has been paused by the server.
        </p>
        <p class="components-resume-failed-visible">
            Failed to resume the session.<br />Please retry or reload the page.
        </p>
        <button id="components-resume-button" class="components-pause-visible components-resume-failed-visible">
            Resume
        </button>
    </div>
</dialog>
